-SL SSR v0.13 - Legacy RGB Response
-=================================
+SL_SSR_v0_14_LegacyDielectricFallback
 
 Purpose
 -------
-This is the first post-plumbing SSR response test after v0.12 proved that
-Firestorm's full-resolution main-pass specularRect reaches the ReShade FX.
+v0.13 proved that valid legacy specularRect.rgb can drive visible SSR once the old alpha/glossiness gate is removed. Raw-hit diagnostics also already prove the ray tracer sees ordinary scene geometry regardless of material response.
 
-v0.13 is FX-only. It requires the v0.12 ReShadePublish add-on to remain
-installed and running.
+v0.14 tests the missing receiver case: legacy opaque surfaces that have neither explicit specular RGB nor classic-shiny/environment intensity.
 
-Change under test
------------------
-Legacy/non-PBR pixels now follow Firestorm's native SSR material use more
-closely:
-
-- specularRect.rgb directly colors the reflected scene contribution;
-- specularRect.a/glossiness is NOT used as a reflectivity gate;
-- classic shiny/environment intensity remains a neutral legacy fallback;
-- PBR weighting is unchanged;
-- ray marcher, scene source, depth, normals, publication path, and composite
-  pipeline are otherwise unchanged.
+What changed
+------------
+FX only. The proven v0.12 native bridge remains installed.
 
-The legacy glossiness UI control is intentionally retained for preset
-compatibility but is labelled unused in v0.13.
+Legacy receiver priority is now:
+  1. explicit Firestorm legacy specularRect.rgb
+  2. classic shiny / environment intensity from the normal G-buffer
+  3. small neutral dielectric fallback only when both signals are absent
 
-Install
--------
-FX-only hot install. Firestorm may remain open.
+Defaults:
+  Legacy No-Spec Threshold = 0.005
+  Legacy No-Spec Fallback  = 0.040
 
-The ReShade technique must visibly read:
-    SL SSR v0.13 - Legacy RGB Response
+The existing view-angle Fresnel still shapes the result, so the fallback is intentionally subtle and becomes strongest toward grazing angles. PBR ORM response is unchanged.
 
-The native SL Probe Lighting overlay will still identify the installed bridge
-as v1.6.10 / v0.12 ReShadePublish because this package does not replace the
-add-on.
-
-Runtime report
+New diagnostic
 --------------
-Use the same legacy/cyan specular test scene. Do NOT press Analyze.
+Display Mode -> Legacy no-spec fallback mask
 
-Return screenshots of:
-1. Display Mode -> SSR contribution
-2. Display Mode -> Final reflection weight x10
-3. Display Mode -> Off (normal composite)
+White = legacy pixel receiving the synthetic fallback.
+Black = explicit legacy specular/classic shiny, PBR, or background.
 
-Interpretation
---------------
-If contribution/weight now appear on legacy pixels with valid specular RGB,
-the old alpha/glossiness gate was the downstream blocker and legacy material
-response is unblocked.
-
-If G-buffer specular RGB remains valid but contribution/weight are still
-black, the next fault is ray/receiver/composite weighting rather than material
-publication.
+Install
+-------
+FX-only package. Firestorm may remain open. Run SL_InstallLatest.ps1 and confirm the technique label reads:
+  SL SSR v0.14 - Legacy Dielectric Fallback
+
+Do not press Analyze.
